The Trilium ETAPI adapter and independent ReadWeave integration are maintained here.
The production ReadWeave project is maintained separately.

Runtime dependencies retain their respective licenses, including PyMuPDF,
Playwright, Beautiful Soup, Requests, jsonschema, markdown-it-py, Pillow,
and tree-sitter-language-pack. Docling is an optional parser integration.
The Codex CLI is installed separately from the official OpenAI distribution.

The architecture viewer bundles Mermaid 10.9.3 under the MIT license.
Its license is preserved in framework/architecture/vendor/LICENSE-mermaid.txt.
The reader also bundles Mermaid and KaTeX 0.16.22 under their retained MIT licenses
in framework/reader/media-vendor.

The repository's examples are self-authored synthetic materials.
User-supplied materials and generated private books are not distributed here.

ReplayWeb.page 2.5.3 is redistributed without modification under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
Its license is preserved in framework/reader/archive/LICENSE-ReplayWeb.page.txt.
